रसिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having juice or sap, juicy, liquid;
tasteful, spirited, full of feeling, impassioned; having
good taste, having a taste for the beautiful.

रस्य, अस्, आ, अम्, juicy, tasty, savoury, palatable;
(आ), f., N. of two plants, = रास्ना; = पाठा; (अम्),
n. blood (supposed to be produced from chyle).

. fr. rt. 1. रस्), a girdle (Ved.; cf. रशना); N.
of two plants, Mimosa Octandra, a thorny shrub;
the ichneumon plant; a sort of perfume.
